{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumLksSshBQvVchuikK3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Mostly yes, with a catch around the name. `Agent` is a Durable Object class (since agents 0.22.0 it extends `DurableObject` directly), so a stub from `env.MY_AGENT.get(env.MY_AGENT.newUniqueId())` can call its public methods over Workers RPC like any other DO. The catch is that the Agents SDK expects every agent instance to have a name. `getAgentByName()` and `routeAgentRequest()` set it for you, but an ID from `newUniqueId()` has no name. Any code path that reads `this.name`, such as connection handling, state broadcasts, scheduling or MCP, may throw because the name was never set.\n\nMy recommendation is to use `getAgentByName(env.MY_AGENT, someId)` with your own unique string, like `crypto.randomUUID()`, instead of `newUniqueId()`. You get a unique instance that still behaves correctly. I answered this from memory and didn't check it against the installed agents 0.27.0, so test your exact case to see whether the unnamed path throws."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9495,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9495},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0999ac5-8beb-4cef-9465-555056f5d234","uuid":"9162a9a3-6bc1-4f5d-a106-b5c4919d701b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:47:56.337Z","request_id":"req_011CfumLkeZMwmaQM6qskVng"}
